#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
run_5model_scorecard.py
=======================
5-model standalone FVS scorecard using FIA remeasurement pairs.

Each configuration is a COMPLETE, internally consistent model system --
DG + HG + crown recession + mortality -- not a mix-and-match of components.

  System 1 - fvs_base      : native FVS (no Greg hooks, no calibration keywords,
                               native varmort mortality)
  System 2 - fvs_regional  : FVS calibration keywords (SDIMAX + BAMAX +
                               BAIMULT + HTGMULT + MORTMULT); no Greg hooks
  System 3 - organon       : Greg DG + Greg HG ORGANON arm
                               (greg_hg_coefficients.csv) + Greg CRW + GOMPIT mort
  System 4 - conus_spdep   : Greg DG + Greg HG compound_none
                               (greg_hg_coefficients_compound_none.csv)
                               + Greg CRW + GOMPIT mort
  System 5 - conus_climate  : Greg DG + Greg HG compound_climate
                               (greg_hg_coefficients_compound_climate.csv)
                               + Greg CRW + GOMPIT mort

Greg DG was trained on NE data; for plots outside NE northern states
(CT/MA/ME/NH/NY/RI/VT) the DG env vars are stripped and calibrated BAIMULT
keywords are injected instead. The model is NOT skipped -- only the DG
component is swapped per plot. All 5 variants (ne/sn/wc/em/pn) run all 5
systems.

Mortality:
  fvs_base    : native FVS varmort (no keywords, no GOMPIT)
  fvs_regional: MORTMULT calibrated keywords (no GOMPIT env var)
  organon / conus_spdep / conus_climate: Greg GOMPIT size+BGI tier
               (FVS_GOMPIT=1 + FVS_GOMPIT_COEF); MORTMULT is NOT emitted
               for these models (GOMPIT fully replaces native mortality).

Usage:
  python3 run_5model_scorecard.py --variant ne [--max-pairs 200] [--seed 42]

Output:
  calibration/output/fia_scorecard/scorecard_{variant}_5model.csv
"""
from __future__ import annotations

